Some Apple Watch users who upgrade to the Series 12 or the Ultra 4 might temporarily lose access to hypertension notifications.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/09/watchos-26-hypertension-alert.jpg" alt="" width="2353" height="1324" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1019925" /><br/>
On the <a href="https://www.apple.com/watchos/feature-availability/">watchOS feature availability page</a>, Apple says notifications might not be available on the Series 12 or Ultra 4 at launch because regulatory clearances are in process.<br/>
<blockquote>Hypertension Notifications may not be available on Apple Watch Series 12 or Ultra 4 in your region, as additional regulatory clearances for these devices are in process.</blockquote><br/>
The warning applies to 33 countries and regions, including Canada, Australia, India, Brazil, Singapore, Japan, Taiwan, South Africa, South Korea, and the UAE, with a full list on Apple's website.<br/>
<br/>
The Apple Watch Series 12 and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-watch-ultra/">Apple Watch Ultra 4</a> have revamped sensors and a new Health Sensing System. Apple added new optical and electrical heart sensors for more frequent and accurate tracking, and the change appears to require new regulatory approval in some locations.<br/>
<br/>
What's new:<br/>
<ul><br/>
 	<li><strong>ECG</strong> - The electrodes in the watch cover more surface area for improved skin contact during ECG readings.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Optical sensing</strong> - Redesigned photodiodes are organized in a ring to capture light more efficiently.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Heart rate measurement</strong> - Larger, power-efficient green LEDs in the optical heart rate sensor allow the new watches to measure heart rate every five seconds all day, offering more data on a user's fitness and physiological state. Real-time heart rate is available in the updated Heart Rate app, and Exercise and Move Activity rings are more accurate. HRV is also measured as often as every five minutes.</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
Apple Watch users who get these notifications today may lose the option when upgrading to the Series 12 or Ultra 4 until regulatory clearance is granted.<br/>
<br/>
